   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the city of Mount\nVernon to impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7321",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7321-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-kk, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7321\n\nSPONSOR: BAILEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the city of\nMount Vernon to impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the\nrepeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo impose a hotel and motel tax rate to benefit the city by providing\nadditional revenues.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection I. Adds a new section 1202-kk to the tax law granting the city\nof Mount Vernon the authority to impose a tax for any hotels, motels,\ntourist homes, motel courts, bed and breakfast establishments, short-\nterm rentals, vacation rentals, Airbnb's clubs or similar facilities.\n\nSection 2. Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe proposed hotel occupancy tax is expected to generate additional\nrevenue for the City of Mount Vernon. These funds will be strategically\nreinvested in critical infrastructure improvements, capital projects,\nand economic development initiatives. Moreover, this tax establishes a\nfair mechanism by ensuring that visitors and tourists, who benefit from\nand place increased demands on essential city services such as public\nsafety, sanitation, and code enforcement, contribute equitably to their\nupkeep. Aligning with regional practices observed in neighboring munici-\npalities, this legislation promotes consistency and fiscal responsibil-\nity across the region.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately, with provisions concerning the act's expiration.\n",
